Mercer Global Advisors, the Denver-headquartered registered investment advisor with $96 billion in assets under management, has hired Melissa Nims, a former Morgan Stanley executive, as its chief solutions officer. She takes over for Jeremiah Barlow, who has been appointed to the newly created chief commercial officer position.&nbsp;

